From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hiroyuki Ikegami <ikegam@mixallow.net>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 14:05:00 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] rtc: s5m: disarm the S2MPG12's WTSR and SMPL restarts at
 power off

On the Pixel 7 Pro (gs201, S2MPG12), power off restarts the phone.
The RTC block read on a running phone shows the PMIC's warm-reset
restart armed:

  0x02 (SMPL) = 0x0e: SMPL_EN 0
  0x03 (WTSR) = 0x0f: WTSR_EN 1, WTSRT 7, COLDRST_EN 0

With WTSR enabled, the PMIC answers the AP dropping power by powering
it up again. Google's S2MPG12 RTC driver clears SMPL_EN, WTSR_EN and
COLDRST_EN in its shutdown callback before every power off, and arms
them again only for a restart (rtc-s2mpg12.c, s2m_rtc_shutdown()).

Do the same for power off and halt. Restarts are left as they are.
This changes power off on the S2MPG12 boards: cheetah, lynx and
panther.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Hiroyuki Ikegami <ikegam@mixallow.net>
---
 drivers/rtc/rtc-s5m.c           | 31 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 include/linux/mfd/samsung/rtc.h |  2 ++
 2 files changed, 33 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/rtc/rtc-s5m.c b/drivers/rtc/rtc-s5m.c
index e38d8b918..dde6d2b81 100644
--- a/drivers/rtc/rtc-s5m.c
+++ b/drivers/rtc/rtc-s5m.c
@@ -709,6 +709,36 @@ static int s5m_rtc_restart_s2mpg10(struct sys_off_data *data)
 	return ret ? NOTIFY_BAD : NOTIFY_DONE;
 }
 
+/*
+ * The PMIC's warm-reset (WTSR, with its cold-reset follow-up) and sudden
+ * power loss (SMPL) restarts stay armed in the always-on RTC block across
+ * boots. Left on, the PMIC answers the AP's power-off by powering it back
+ * up, so power off turns into a restart. Google's S2MPG12 RTC driver turns
+ * all three off in its shutdown callback before every power off, and arms
+ * them again only for a restart (rtc-s2mpg12.c, s2m_rtc_shutdown()).
+ * Restarts are left alone here: they never needed it on gs201.
+ */
+static void s5m_rtc_shutdown(struct platform_device *pdev)
+{
+	struct s5m_rtc_info *info = platform_get_drvdata(pdev);
+	int ret;
+
+	if (info->device_type != S2MPG12)
+		return;
+
+	if (system_state != SYSTEM_POWER_OFF && system_state != SYSTEM_HALT)
+		return;
+
+	ret = regmap_clear_bits(info->regmap, S2MPG10_RTC_SMPL,
+				S2MPG10_SMPL_EN);
+	if (!ret)
+		ret = regmap_clear_bits(info->regmap, S2MPG10_RTC_WTSR,
+					S2MPG10_WTSR_COLDRST |
+					S2MPG10_WTSR_WTSR_EN);
+	if (ret)
+		dev_err(info->dev, "failed to disarm WTSR/SMPL: %d\n", ret);
+}
+
 static int s5m_rtc_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 {
 	struct sec_pmic_dev *s5m87xx = dev_get_drvdata(pdev->dev.parent);
@@ -874,6 +904,7 @@ static struct platform_driver s5m_rtc_driver = {
 		.pm	= &s5m_rtc_pm_ops,
 	},
 	.probe		= s5m_rtc_probe,
+	.shutdown	= s5m_rtc_shutdown,
 	.id_table	= s5m_rtc_id,
 };
 
diff --git a/include/linux/mfd/samsung/rtc.h b/include/linux/mfd/samsung/rtc.h
index 51c4239a1..5dbbbd1f6 100644
--- a/include/linux/mfd/samsung/rtc.h
+++ b/include/linux/mfd/samsung/rtc.h
@@ -167,4 +167,6 @@ enum s2mpg10_rtc_reg {
 #define S2MPG10_WTSR_WTSRT	GENMASK(3, 1)
 #define S2MPG10_WTSR_WTSR_EN	BIT(0)
 
+#define S2MPG10_SMPL_EN		BIT(0)
+
 #endif /*  __LINUX_MFD_SEC_RTC_H */
